## UI polish: Notification settings card

13 fixes across spacing, typography, contrast, hierarchy, layout and states. Text and brand hue kept.

### Fixes
1. **Spacing**: card `padding: 13px` is off the scale. Now `padding: 12px`. (R-ui-polish-1)
2. **Spacing**: heading `margin: 0 0 5px` is off the scale. Now `margin: 0 0 4px`. (R-ui-polish-1)
3. **Spacing**: button `padding: 6px 10px` is off the scale. Now `padding: 8px 12px`. (R-ui-polish-1)
4. **Typography**: heading `font-size: 22px` is off the scale. Now `font-size: 24px`. (R-ui-polish-2)
5. **Typography**: description `font-size: 13px` is off the scale and below the 16px body minimum. Now `font-size: 16px`. (R-ui-polish-2)
6. **Typography**: buttons used the browser default size (about 13.33px), which is off the scale. Now `font-size: 16px; font-family: inherit`. (R-ui-polish-2)
7. **Typography**: the heading had no line-height. Now `line-height: 1.2`. (R-ui-polish-3)
8. **Typography**: the description had no line-height and no width limit. Now `line-height: 1.5; max-width: 65ch`. (R-ui-polish-3)
9. **Contrast**: `#aaaaaa` on `#ffffff` is 2.32:1. Now `#747474`, 4.67:1, which is the same grey hue. (R-ui-polish-4)
10. **Hierarchy**: both buttons were filled `#2563eb`, so there were two primary actions. "Save changes" stays filled. "Cancel" is now an outline button: `background: #ffffff; color: #2563eb; border: 1px solid #2563eb`. Both buttons get a 1px border so they are the same height. (R-ui-polish-5)
11. **Layout**: the buttons had no minimum target size. Now `min-height: 44px; min-width: 44px`. (R-ui-polish-7)
12. **States**: the buttons had no hover style. Now the primary hover is `background: #1d4ed8`, and the secondary hover is `color` and `border-color: #1d4ed8`. (R-ui-polish-6)
13. **States**: the buttons had no focus or disabled style. Now `:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid #2563eb; outline-offset: 2px }` and `:disabled { opacity: 0.5; cursor: not-allowed }`. (R-ui-polish-6)

### Contrast
| Text | Before | After |
|------|--------|-------|
| Card description | #aaaaaa on #ffffff, 2.32:1 | #747474 on #ffffff, 4.67:1 |
| Save changes | #ffffff on #2563eb, 5.17:1 | #ffffff on #2563eb, 5.17:1 (hover #ffffff on #1d4ed8, 6.70:1) |
| Cancel | #ffffff on #2563eb, 5.17:1 | #2563eb on #ffffff, 5.17:1 (hover #1d4ed8 on #ffffff, 6.70:1) |

Ratios computed with the contrast script.

### Polished code
```html
<style>
  .card { padding: 12px; background: #ffffff; font-family: system-ui; }
  .card h2 { font-size: 24px; line-height: 1.2; margin: 0 0 4px; }
  .card p { font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; max-width: 65ch; color: #747474; }
  .card .btn {
    min-height: 44px;
    min-width: 44px;
    padding: 8px 12px;
    font-size: 16px;
    font-family: inherit;
    border: 1px solid #2563eb;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .card .btn-primary { background: #2563eb; color: #fff; }
  .card .btn-primary:hover { background: #1d4ed8; border-color: #1d4ed8; }
  .card .btn-secondary { background: #ffffff; color: #2563eb; }
  .card .btn-secondary:hover { color: #1d4ed8; border-color: #1d4ed8; }
  .card .btn:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid #2563eb; outline-offset: 2px; }
  .card .btn:disabled { opacity: 0.5; cursor: not-allowed; }
</style>
<div class="card">
  <h2>Notification settings</h2>
  <p>Choose how we contact you about your account.</p>
  <button class="btn btn-primary">Save changes</button>
  <button class="btn btn-secondary">Cancel</button>
</div>
```

### Not changed
- All visible text, word for word.
- Brand hue kept: #2563eb (hover shade #1d4ed8 has the same hue).
- Card background #ffffff and font family system-ui.
- Font weights: two (heading bold, everything else regular).

### Open questions
- Inline styles can't hold hover, focus or disabled states, so the styles were moved into a `<style>` block with new classes (`btn`, `btn-primary`, `btn-secondary`). Should these go into your main stylesheet instead?
- "Save changes" was made the primary action and "Cancel" the secondary one. Is that the order you want?
